  <section class="wrap band fit">
    <div>
      <h2>Models</h2>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>Qwen3.5-family hybrid text models, including Qwen3.8 and, experimentally, the Qwen3.6 mixture-of-experts</li>
        <li>Gemma 4 text, with WAV audio on E2B and E4B</li>
        <li>gpt-oss text, through the expert cache when it doesn't fit</li>
        <li>Whisper large-v3-turbo for transcription</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/docs/design/scope/#validation-status">How far each model has been validated</a></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>When to look elsewhere</h2>
      <p>Tur supports few models and doesn't accept images or video. It has no embeddings, serves one chat model per process, and its HTTP API doesn't offer structured output yet. On 8K-token prompts, llama.cpp prefills 6 to 11% faster on a 16 GB M1.</p>
      <p>For those, or for other hardware, look at oMLX, llama.cpp, Ollama, SGLang or Strata. <a href="/docs/architecture/comparison/">Tur and other engines</a> says which fits what.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

